IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pra71-rules`

-- Independent tests, written from BRIEF.md and the Act before reading the rules.
-- See independent-expectations.md for the working.

GIVEN c IS A `Pension class 1971`
      amt IS A NUMBER
      hus IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Increase position 1971`
`pos` c amt hus MEANS
    `the increase position for` (`Pensioner 1971` OF c, amt, hus, (Date 14 10 1971))

GIVEN c IS A `Pension class 1971`
      amt IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`inc` c amt MEANS (`pos` c amt 0)'s `the increase`

-- s 3(1)
#ASSERT `inc` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` 48.16 EQUALS JUST 13.98
#ASSERT `inc` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` 56.89 EQUALS JUST 16.78
#ASSERT `inc` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` 57.79 EQUALS JUST 16.78
#ASSERT `inc` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` 63.79 EQUALS JUST 16.78
#ASSERT `inc` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` 50 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(2)
#ASSERT (`pos` `a widow under s 3(2)` 0 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 62.14
-- s 4
#ASSERT `inc` `an annual pensioner under s 4` 2729.17 EQUALS JUST 729.16
#ASSERT `inc` `an annual pensioner under s 4` 3275 EQUALS JUST 875
#ASSERT `inc` `an annual pensioner under s 4` 3587.86 EQUALS JUST 875
#ASSERT `inc` `an annual pensioner under s 4` 2916.67 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`pos` `a widow under s 4(2)` 0 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 3458.33
-- s 5
#ASSERT `inc` `an annual pensioner under s 5` 2916.67 EQUALS JUST 729.16
#ASSERT `inc` `an annual pensioner under s 5` 3500 EQUALS JUST 875
#ASSERT `inc` `an annual pensioner under s 5` 3812.86 EQUALS JUST 875
#ASSERT (`pos` `a widow under s 5(2)` 0 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 3645.83
-- s 6(1)
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder under s 6` 15 EQUALS JUST 7.12
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder under s 6` 18 EQUALS JUST 8.54
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder under s 6` 20 EQUALS JUST 10.33
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder under s 6` 23.33 EQUALS JUST 11.36
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder under s 6` 28 EQUALS JUST 13.63
-- s 6(2): five-sixths of the husband's increase, exact
#ASSERT (`pos` `a widow under s 6(2)` 0 28)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST (1363 DIVIDED BY 120)
#ASSERT (`pos` `a widow under s 6(2)` 0 18)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST (427 DIVIDED BY 60)
#ASSERT (`pos` `a widow under s 6(2)` 0 19)'s `the increase` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder or widow under s 7` 1050 EQUALS JUST 183.75
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder or widow under s 7` 1260 EQUALS JUST 220.5
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder or widow under s 7` 2500 EQUALS JUST 437.5
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder or widow under s 7` 3000 EQUALS JUST 525
#ASSERT `inc` `an office-holder or widow under s 7` 2000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8: one-half
#ASSERT `inc` `a former Prime Minister's widow under s 8` 1000 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `inc` `a former Prime Minister's widow under s 8` 1234.57 EQUALS JUST (123457 DIVIDED BY 200)
-- outside the classes
#ASSERT `inc` `none of these` 48.16 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12: from the first fortnightly payment
#ASSERT (`pos` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` 48.16 0)'s `from` EQUALS JUST (Date 14 10 1971)
#ASSERT (`pos` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` 50 0)'s `from` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12 does not apply to the fixed widow rates in ss 3(2), 4(2), 5(2)
#ASSERT (`pos` `a widow under s 3(2)` 0 0)'s `from` EQUALS NOTHING
